WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.120
There are quite a few rotating
buildings in the world,

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.580
houses for people who want their
view to follow the sun.

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:08.040
Maybe they're built as an
architect's dream house,

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.600
maybe as an engineering challenge,

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.780
or sometimes to give the
best angles for solar power.

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:15.600
Over the years, I have asked to
film in a few of those houses,

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.640
but I've always been turned down.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:20.220
They're private homes.
But this one,

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:23.280
near San Diego, California,
is now on sale.

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:24.840
The real estate agent
got in touch

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:26.220
and asked if I wanted
to have a look around.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:28.740
To be clear,
this is not an advert.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:29.640
They're not paying me.

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:31.620
But I just wasn't going
to turn this down.

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:34.140
Because there are two things
I want to find out.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:37.260
First of all, how on earth
does the plumbing work?

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:39.600
And second, if this is
someone's dream house,

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:40.500
and it is,

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.260
then why are they
selling it?

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:45.960
- My wife and I decided we're
going to build a house.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:49.440
Just so happened, this lot went
on the market that same day.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.120
We happened to see the sign,

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:52.260
we bought it.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.240
I'm trying to figure out
what to build.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:57.420
I said, you know,
why not a round house?

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:00.120
That way, more rooms
will have more view.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.220
And my wife said, fine.

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:05.580
Then I thought, some rooms still
have to look at the mountain.

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:08.820
So I said,
why don't we rotate it?

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:11.640
To my surprise,
she said, fine!

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:14.820
And I thought, crap, I've got to
figure out how to do that!

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:19.140
So I started to figure out
how to actually build

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:23.100
something that would rotate, so
every room would have every view.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:26.660
- Yes, of course I asked if I could
flip the switch and control the rotation.

00:01:31.881 --> 00:01:33.319
- Go up to a thousand.

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:36.060
Good.

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:38.578
That's it.

00:01:38.578 --> 00:01:42.300
- It's very strange to push a button
and then have the world

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:43.738
start to rotate around you.
- That's right!

00:01:43.738 --> 00:01:44.370
- That's lovely.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:47.640
- My wife and I started
construction in 2000.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:51.300
It took a good two years
to get to the point

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:53.100
where we had a structure.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:56.220
We did hire some people and
had them working here,

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:59.220
and I found that they would
go home at four o'clock

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:02.040
and I would be here 'til seven
fixing what they had done,

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:05.940
because they're used to building square
and this was round.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:10.620
The fella at San Diego County
would go over our plans

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:12.120
and he says, "I just
want to tell you,

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:16.140
"you're building something that's
way stronger than it needs to be.

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:19.440
"No way you can rotate that much
mass and and have it work."

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:22.500
So I said, "do you care
if it rotates?"

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:25.440
He says, "hell, I don't care
if it rotates".

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:28.200
And I said, "well then can we
just agree to disagree

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:30.480
"and you let me go ahead
and build the damn thing?"

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.220
And he said "all right".

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:34.020
In doing all the calculations,

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:37.560
I came up with needing a
five-horsepower motor,

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:40.740
so I put in
a five-horsepower motor.

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:44.340
Have you ever driven your car
in fifth gear at 25mph?

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:48.780
It goes like that, and that's
how the house was moving.

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:51.600
Cut it down to a one-and-a-half
horsepower motor.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:55.620
It goes through a 25:1
reduction transmission,

00:02:55.620 --> 00:03:01.800
a 71:1 torque hub that drives
the two 16-inch diameter wheels.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:04.800
We can turn the
house in 45 minutes.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:07.620
You can go to bed to the sunset,

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.540
and wake up to the sunrise
in the same bed.

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:14.220
You have guests over, during dinner,
we'll turn the house so that

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:16.470
everybody at the dinner table
gets to see the sunset.

00:03:16.470 --> 00:03:20.400
- In a lot of rotating buildings,
it's only part of the floor that rotates.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.740
the things that require plumbing,
like the kitchen and bathroom,

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:23.640
don't move at all.

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:26.880
But here, the sinks and toilets
and electrical sockets

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:28.560
all rotate as part of the house,

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:31.980
and all the explanations I can find
seem to hand-wave the details.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:35.040
They just say that there's a
central non-rotating core

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:36.480
that handles the pipes.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:39.180
For electricity, there are
off-the-shelf components

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:40.080
that can deal with rotation.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:42.360
- There's a thing called a slip ring.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:44.520
Which is a very standard
piece of equipment.

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:46.140
Just like a merry-go-round.

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:48.420
A merry-go-round goes around
and around and around,

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:50.040
and it doesn't have to go backwards.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:53.160
Same thing here.
It happens to be a fancy one,

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:57.240
16 brushes that go around a
copper piece about that big,

00:03:57.240 --> 00:04:02.160
and they ride on the copper
and that is your connection.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:05.460
- For telephone and internet, there's
also an off-the-shelf component.

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:09.300
A mercury slip ring, a sealed connector
with a small pool of mercury,

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:10.920
conductive liquid metal,
in the center.

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:12.480
Both sides can rotate.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:14.400
They just stay connected to the liquid.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.260
But that's not the difficult part.

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:19.080
I can understand having one connection
going through the middle,

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:21.000
for water or wastewater or gas.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.280
They can just sit on a
central pipe and swivel.

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:26.460
But how can you have all three
going through the same central hub?

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:29.640
The topology doesn't work.
They can't all occupy the exact center.

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:32.100
But if they're offset,
then as the house rotates,

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:35.400
surely the lengths of the pipes
and cables has to change?

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:37.860
Or if there's slack, surely
they'll get twisted.

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:41.040
Turns out Al has a very clever
solution to that.

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:42.900
- Obviously you don't want to mix

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:46.200
the gas, the gray water,
the sewer, the drinking water.

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:50.580
So I designed a slip ring
for those services.

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:53.700
Big piece of steel,
about that big around.

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:57.240
This is fixed. We grooved it,

00:04:57.240 --> 00:05:00.060
it's about a 3" by 3" groove
all the way around.

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:04.200
Top groove is sewer.
The next groove is gray water.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:07.980
The next groove is drinking water.
The bottom groove is gas.

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:12.960
And there are holes drilled
through this from the sewer,

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:14.280
from the gray water and so forth,

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:17.040
They're all separate holes
that come out the bottom.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:21.060
Then there's a piece that
comes down the outside.

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:24.360
This piece rotates with the house.

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:30.240
You have a sewer line that comes down
and connects to the outer piece,

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:34.080
and then you have gray water,
then you have drinking water,

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:35.040
then you have gas.

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:39.960
There are seals inbetween
each of these grooves.

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:41.820
They're all alarmed.

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:44.700
There's a seal, a sensor ring,
and a seal.

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:47.520
A seal, a sensor ring,
and a seal,

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:49.140
so forth for all of them.

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:52.920
You would have to have two seals
and two sensors fail

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:55.680
before you had any mixture of fluids

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:58.200
The seals are good for 75 years,

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:00.840
so I don't think we're gonna have a problem!

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:03.660
- Yes, I had to commission
some graphics to explain this.

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:05.940
It's really clever
and I did not understand it

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:07.140
until Al explained it to me.

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:09.480
It's like four intersecting funnels.

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:15.120
- The total maintenance, once a year,
is to lube the bearings.

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:19.320
We have a young man who has
done it several times.

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:21.120
It's done in an hour.

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:23.400
- Which brings me to the
other big question I had.

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:25.260
After designing and constructing
this place,

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:27.000
after 20 years of living here,

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:28.800
why sell it?

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:32.100
- I've had 18 heart procedures.

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:34.620
My wife is in perfect health.

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:39.000
The odds of me outliving her
are zero.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.760
She was born and raised in Coronado.

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:44.820
We're moving back to Coronado.

00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:49.800
Because this is a complex house,
even though I think it's simple!

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:54.780
For her to try and teach somebody else
how to run everything and do everything

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:57.840
would be difficult
if something happened to me.

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:00.600
So we're just kind of jumping ahead.

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:02.820
And Coronado's a pretty nice place to go.

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:04.740
- Will this place sell quickly?

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:07.020
I don't know.
I'm not a real estate agent,

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:08.820
but I certainly hope that
there'll be people

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:11.040
who want to live somewhere
with this view

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:13.320
in a home that's this different.

